(J,"Then polished, then coated with the body's gloss black coating in the same coating batch as the body HSG1 (17.29; specs/body.md).","Then polished, then coated with the body's gloss black coating (Oerlikon Balzers BALINIT DLC, black, 1 to 3 um, applied under 250 degrees C; it adds at most 0.003 mm per face, which the 0.10 mm bond gap takes) in the same coating batch as the body HSG1 (17.29; specs/body.md; item 105).",LD+"'item 105 (coating thickness)' 2026-11-13 04:15"),
(J,"- FRM1 into the body: bonded with DP420 Black, 0.10 mm radial gap, cured 24 h at 22 C before the cap goes in","- FRM1 into the body: the bond faces are abraded and cleaned with isopropyl alcohol first (3M sheet, surface preparation E; item 106), then bonded with DP420 Black, 0.10 mm radial gap, cured 24 h at 22 C before the cap goes in",LD+"'item 106' 2026-11-13 03:56"),
(J,"- coating colour, gloss and adhesion, the same acceptance as the body (body.md);","- coating colour, gloss and adhesion, the same acceptance as the body (body.md); five lap-shear strips of coated Ti-6Al-4V from the same coating batch, bonded and pulled: the break is inside the adhesive, not at the coating (a break at the coating means the bond faces are masked before coating; item 106);",LD+"'item 106'"),
(J,"6. Bench items B6 (centre press) and B9 (feel, sealing, wear of the coating) can change this part.","6. Bench items B6 (centre press: ONE switch, SW2, under the cap's centre; force at the click 1.1 to 2.1 N and travel 0.06 to 0.16 mm at the cap's centre, Alps sheet page 2; never press above 2.1 N; item 100) and B9 (feel, sealing, wear of the coating) can change this part.",LD+"'item 100' 2026-11-13 03:56"),
(J,"7. The joystick opening relies on the switches' own rating (IP6X and IPX7) and the dam DAM1 for water; dam material and the stiffener material are open item S26 (assembly.md section 5).","7. The joystick opening relies on the switches' own rating (IP6X and IPX7) and the dam DAM1 for water; version 1 claims no water or dust rating (item 101; the build guide holds one optional test, 1 m of water for 30 minutes, then open and look: its result is recorded, it is not a pass line). Dam material is open item S26 (assembly.md section 5); the stiffener is polyimide, 0.10 (band-flex-tails.md).",LD+"'item 101' 2026-11-13 03:56; model v8 stiffener"),

(G,"(model v5; assembly.md step 23, conflict K-A4; architecture 17.23, 17.24; open item S26). The tape is not chosen and its compressed thickness is unknown.","(model v5; assembly.md step 23, conflict K-A4; architecture 17.23, 17.24). SEAL1 is a ring of tesa 61305 double-sided film, 50 um (bond to glass 12.4 N/cm); its sheet states no value for coated titanium and none for water: on the first body a bond check after 24 hours, then a water spray test; version 1 claims no water rating (item 110).",LD+"'item 110 (glass seal SEAL1)' 2026-11-13 04:15"),
(G,"bonded to the screen panel by 0.1 mm clear adhesive (ADH1) over the whole face,","bonded to the screen panel by 0.1 mm clear adhesive (ADH1, tesa 69404, optically clear, 100 um, haze under 0.5 percent) over the whole face,",LD+"'item 96, rest (screen stack)' 04:15"),
(G,"Default, to confirm with the maker: chemically strengthened aluminosilicate glass. Reason: thin formed glass that can be strengthened. Brand, grade and the strengthening depth and surface stress: open point 1.","AGC Dragontrail Pro, chemically strengthened (surface stress 1000 MPa, depth 40 um), density 2.46: the glass weighs 0.82 g (332.87 cubic mm). Reason: thin formed glass that can be strengthened. Its sheet gives no thickness range and no forming limit (open point 2). The ring's weight is measured on the first unit, part by part, on a 0.01 g balance (items 107 to 109).",LD+"'items 107, 108, 109' 2026-11-13 04:15"),
(G,"Whether one can form an arc of 30.7 mm with 1.0 mm and 1.2 mm rolls at 1.10 mm thickness, and the forming tolerance: open point 2.","Whether a maker can form an arc of 30.7 mm with 1.0 mm and 1.2 mm rolls at 1.10 mm thickness, and the forming tolerance: open point 2; it is shown only by the first formed sample (thickness at 5 points with a micrometer, radius with a gauge; items 107 to 109).",LD+"'items 107, 108, 109'"),
(G,"| clear adhesive ADH1 | 0.10 mm | open point 2 | glass to screen panel over the whole face (17.2, 17.30) |","| clear adhesive ADH1 | 0.10 mm | open point 2 | glass to screen panel over the whole face (17.2, 17.30); tesa 69404, 100 um (item 96, rest) |",LD+"'item 96, rest (screen stack)'"),
(G,"| glass seal ring SEAL1 | 0.05 mm thick | open | perimeter ring","| glass seal ring SEAL1 | 0.05 mm thick | open | tesa 61305 film, 50 um (item 110); perimeter ring",LD+"'item 110'"),
(G,"1. Glass brand and grade, strengthening depth and stress: the glass maker proposes.","1. Glass: AGC Dragontrail Pro, chemically strengthened, surface stress 1000 MPa, depth 40 um (items 107 to 109); the glass former (a maker that can form it) is still to be found.",LD+"'items 107, 108, 109'"),
(G,"4. Seal: the seal tape and its compressed thickness (S26). (Before v7","4. Seal: tesa 61305, 50 um (item 110); whether it holds on coated titanium and against water is measured on the first body. (Before v7",LD+"'item 110'"),
